{"kind":"request","text":"Pin the citation half of resolveReviewed, or stop claiming it. At internal/workroom/fold.go:1197 in commit 2f394f327dfa3fc2a6bbfd7a9a24922f529386e2, the named-artifact path requires both that the artifact stands at the claimed head and that the report rests on it: judgesTheClaimedHead(basis.named) \u0026\u0026 contains(basis.restsOn, basis.named). Deleting the contains clause leaves the entire test tree green, measured by the integrator with go test ./... at that head. Every case that exercises the citation also fails the head check, so the citation is never the deciding condition anywhere. The function's own comment states the property the tests do not hold - that a name in the body is a label the reviewer typed and only the citation makes it a link the log can follow - so the code documents a guarantee nothing enforces. The gap is inherited from reviewed head d38ccd8ac42e202c33792fe80958551f8977d544 and is not a merge regression.","body":{"conditions":"A test names an artifact that stands at the claimed head but is not among the report's bases, and fails when the contains clause is deleted while passing when it is restored, demonstrated by applying that single deletion alone and reverting it. If instead the citation is judged not to be load-bearing, the comment at internal/workroom/fold.go:1180-1187 is corrected to state only what the code enforces, and that correction rests on the artifact for this behaviour. Either way go vet, go test and race are green, and the change is approved at an exact head by a reviewer other than the author.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}